  "findings": [
    "Read the unchanged original D/DC/try helpers, all ten original expected path literals, surrounding searchpath/require/cache/reload/native prefix assertions and complete named Windows counterpart. The template substitutes the native directory separator; original hardcoded slash expectations disagree with the same-host C baseline before the later body.",
    "Use D only where the original template contains that native separator. The P1 init template deliberately retains its literal slash suffix: libs..dirsep..P1/init.lua. Never normalize the actual loader output. Both exact loader data and module values remain required.",
    "All ten changes affect only expected platform path literals. No assertion, port guard, T call, module function or cleanup is removed. Binary Lua-module loading, native entry-name resolution, cached truthy modules and repeated false-result loading remain actual behavior under test.",
    "The standalone .lc counterpart uses text to exercise path selection only. It does not replace original attrib binary-chunk assertions; the full transformed file and actual C fixtures remain mandatory.",
    "Approve source generation in disposable directories for Windows only, in both configurations. This decision supplies no native applicability or passing execution evidence. Each final context requires unchanged original C failure capture, actual same-image fixture/linkage counterpart, complete transformed C/Ada return27 protocol, cleanup and separately reviewed applicability.",
    "No exemption applies to Linux/macOS; their original source remains required. Final whole-target authority cannot be inferred from this source-only mapping."
  ],
